@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@userId = customer-mahesh
@conversationId = conv-return-policy

### ===================================================================
### STAGE 11 — AGENTIC ORCHESTRATION VERIFICATION
### ===================================================================

### Query 1: Compound Multi-Intent (Tool Calling + Policy RAG + Memory)
### Expected:
### 1. Calls OrderStatusTool for SK-1042 (status: DELAYED / OUT_FOR_DELIVERY)
### 2. Retrieves shipping-policy.txt via ChromaDB to find delay compensation
### 3. Synthesizes a unified response addressing status AND delay compensation
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/agent/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "{{userId}}",
  "conversationId": "{{conversationId}}-q1",
  "message": "I'm Liam Chen from Singapore. My order SK-1002 hasn't arrived yet. Can you check its status and tell me if it's covered under the delay policy?"
}

###

### Query 2: Product Discovery + Return Policy Check
### Expected:
### 1. Calls ProductInfoTool to check stock and price of 'Beard Trimmer Pro'
### 2. Retrieves return-policy.txt to verify if trimmers have a 14-day window
### 3. Answers both purchase feasibility and return eligibility
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/agent/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "{{userId}}",
  "conversationId": "{{conversationId}}-q2",
  "message": "Is the Beard Trimmer Pro in stock, and what is its return window if I don't like it?"
}

###

### Query 3: Graceful Degrade / Single-Step Policy Question
### Expected: Verifies the agent doesn't hallucinate tools when only RAG is needed
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/agent/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "{{userId}}",
  "conversationId": "{{conversationId}}-q3",
  "message": "What is your standard cancellation policy if I cancel an order within 2 hours?"
}

###

### Query 4: Conversational Continuity Under Agent Orchestration
### Expected: Recalls the context of SK-1042 from Query 1 without re-specifying the order ID
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/agent/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "{{userId}}",
  "conversationId": "{{conversationId}}-q1",
  "message": "When was that order originally expected to be delivered?"
}

